 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Concept Testing Survey FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a concept testing survey?\", \"a\": \"A concept testing survey shows people a product or ad idea before launch and records how they react: whether they would buy it and what they would change. Concept testing is an early-stage market research method, run before money goes into building the idea.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a concept testing survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe the concepts, the people you want to hear from, and the questions to ask after each concept in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>. Emergent builds the survey, the screener and cell logic, and a database for every answer. Try it with a few people from your target, then send the link to your panel or customer list.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good concept testing survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good ones use plain wording and a fixed answer scale for each question. After every concept, ask how likely the person is to buy it, how different it is from what they buy now, and how believable its main claim is. Add a price question only when the concept shows a price, and keep the wording identical across concepts.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some concept testing survey examples?\", \"a\": \"Here are four. A package test shows each shopper one of 3 designs. A feature test has customers rate 4 ideas in random order. A tagline test checks ad copy, and a counter test asks coffee customers about a new drink. Each asks about something that does not exist yet, unlike a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/wellness'>wellness survey</a>, which tracks habits people already have. Swap in your own concepts in the prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many respondents do concept testing surveys need per concept?\", \"a\": \"Plan for at least 100 qualified answers per cell, and 200 if you want to compare groups such as regions inside a cell. In a monadic test that number applies to each concept: 3 concepts at 200 each means 600 people. Emergent puts no cap on responses, and the cell size is limited only by the people you can reach.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a concept testing survey be monadic or sequential monadic?\", \"a\": \"Pick monadic if you can reach enough people to give every concept its own group, and sequential monadic if you cannot. In a monadic test, respondents complete a full evaluation of a single concept. In a sequential monadic test, respondents complete full evaluations for multiple concepts, and the order of concepts is randomized to reduce the odds of bias.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a concept testing survey different from a broader study of the market?\", \"a\": \"A concept testing survey answers one narrow question: how do people react to this specific idea? A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/market-research'>market research survey</a> covers the market around it, such as who buys in the category and why they switch brands. Run the broader study first to find the gap, then a concept test to check the idea that fills it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should a concept testing survey screen out?\", \"a\": \"Screen out anyone who has not bought in the category in the past 90 days, plus anyone who works in market research or for a competing brand. Screening questions help ensure respondents fit the target audience of the concept. Put them before any concept appears. Screened-out rows stay in a database you own, which shows how many people on your list qualified.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I read concept testing survey results?\", \"a\": \"Start with the share in each cell who picked the top two answers on the purchase question, and compare shares rather than raw counts. Then check appeal and believability for the top 2 concepts, and read the open answers for what to fix. A concept that feels new but scores low on believability needs clearer proof before it goes further.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a needs assessment come before a concept testing survey?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when you do not yet know which problem to solve. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/needs-assessment'>needs assessment survey</a> asks people what they lack or struggle with, and a concept test then checks whether your answer to that gap lands. Emergent builds both from a prompt, and the concept test can reuse the screener from the first study.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 },
